{"id": "1473586105", "uploader": "Ocean Networks Canada", "uploader_id": "65324226", "uploader_url": "https://soundcloud.com/oceannetworkscanada", "timestamp": 1679347062, "title": "Bigg's orcas at Folger Passage", "track": "Bigg's orcas at Folger Passage", "description": "Our Folger Deep hydrophone picked up this unusual orca vocalization event on March 13, 2023. Identified as Bigg’s orcas (aka Transient orcas), they were heard calling for an hour and a half! This is unusual because they are typically silent to avoid alerting their prey - seals, sea lions, and other whales. To further this mystery, these Bigg’s orcas were using “aberrant” calls, a highly modified version of their typical calls. Aberrant calls are associated with socialization in resident orcas so we’re not quite sure what this means for Bigg’s orcas!\n\nwww.oceannetworks.ca\n\nOriginal file: ICLISTENHF1266_20230313T025000.084Z_20230313T025500.084Z-OD.WAV", "thumbnails": [{"id": "mini", "url": "https://i1.sndcdn.com/artworks-VFYPyqwZQLl8gxIA-QO1Cuw-mini.jpg", "width": 16, "height": 16, "resolution": "16x16"}, {"id": "tiny", "url": "https://i1.sndcdn.com/artworks-VFYPyqwZQLl8gxIA-QO1Cuw-tiny.jpg", "width": 20, "height": 20, "resolution": "20x20"}, {"id": "small", "url": "https://i1.sndcdn.com/artworks-VFYPyqwZQLl8gxIA-QO1Cuw-small.jpg", "width": 32, "height": 32, "resolution": "32x32"}, {"id": "badge", "url": "https://i1.sndcdn.com/artworks-VFYPyqwZQLl8gxIA-QO1Cuw-badge.jpg", "width": 47, "height": 47, "resolution": "47x47"}, {"id": "t67x67", "url": "https://i1.sndcdn.com/artworks-VFYPyqwZQLl8gxIA-QO1Cuw-t67x67.jpg", "width": 67, "height": 67, "resolution": "67x67"}, {"id": "large", "url": "https://i1.sndcdn.com/artworks-VFYPyqwZQLl8gxIA-QO1Cuw-large.jpg", "width": 100, "height": 100, "resolution": "100x100"}, {"id": "t300x300", "url": "https://i1.sndcdn.com/artworks-VFYPyqwZQLl8gxIA-QO1Cuw-t300x300.jpg", "width": 300, "height": 300, "resolution": "300x300"}, {"id": "crop", "url": "https://i1.sndcdn.